==============================================================================
Vercel env-var alignment + API_BASE_URL fix — Production + Preview
==============================================================================
Date:          2026-05-12
Operator:      shoaibrain
Git SHA:       ad1a194 (frontend, edforge-saas-frontend@main; merge of PR #45)
Sprint:        grade-level-fix T1 (deploy ladder side-effect cleanup)
Doc ref:       docs/infrastructure-sunset/sprint-4-vercel-env-update.md
Reason:        Close out infra-sunset/4 T4.3.3 (Preview env vars) + defuse the
               API_BASE_URL='' time-bomb that would have broken edforge.app on
               the next rebuild.

==============================================================================
Background
==============================================================================
infra-sunset/4 documented updating Vercel env vars for both Production and
Preview to point at the new ap-south-1 prod stack. Production was updated on
2026-05-03 but **Preview was missed** for 9 days. The miss surfaced during
grade-level-fix T1 when PR #45's preview URL failed with:
  "User pool client f9r69qrqfgpekdjfo93a8n5mu does not exist"
— the dead UAT us-east-2 Cognito client ID was still cached in Preview env.

While fixing Preview, found a second issue: API_BASE_URL=='' (empty) in
Production env. The currently-deployed bundle worked because its routing
manifest had the value baked at build time, but ANY rebuild would have shipped
a broken bundle (axios receiving SPA index.html instead of JSON, app stuck on
Loading). See sprint-4 doc § "If something's wrong" for full failure-mode
write-up.

==============================================================================
Actions taken
==============================================================================

# 1. Pull current Production snapshot (read-only, sanity check)
vercel env pull --environment=production /tmp/vercel-prod-snapshot.env
  -> revealed API_BASE_URL=""  (the time-bomb)

# 2. Preview environment — 7 vars updated to match Production values
#    (executed as a single bash for-loop; output condensed here)
for VAR in VITE_COGNITO_REGION VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID \
           VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID VITE_API_URL VITE_REDIRECT_SIGN_IN \
           VITE_REDIRECT_SIGN_OUT API_BASE_URL; do
  vercel env rm  "$VAR" preview --yes
  printf '%s' "$VALUE_FROM_PROD_SNAPSHOT" | vercel env add "$VAR" preview
done
  -> all 7 rm/add cycles ✅ Removed/Added Environment Variable (per CLI output)
  -> API_BASE_URL initially skipped due to empty prod value; corrected in step 3

# 3. API_BASE_URL Production + Preview — corrected to the real backend URL
vercel env rm API_BASE_URL production --yes
echo -n "https://w5ulch7iyf.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/prod" \
  | vercel env add API_BASE_URL production
  -> ✅ Removed Environment Variable
  -> ✅ Added Environment Variable API_BASE_URL to Project edforge-saas-frontend

echo -n "https://w5ulch7iyf.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/prod" \
  | vercel env add API_BASE_URL preview
  -> ✅ Added Environment Variable API_BASE_URL to Project edforge-saas-frontend

# 4. Trigger Preview rebuild (empty commit on PR #45 branch)
git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: rebuild after API_BASE_URL alignment"
git push
  -> Vercel built Preview deployment jfnvv8hkf in 21s, status Ready

# 5. PR #45 merged (no force-push; rebased earlier onto current main)
gh pr merge 45 --rebase
  -> merge commit ad1a194 on edforge-saas-frontend@main

# 6. Production auto-rebuilt via Vercel main-branch hook
  -> Vercel built Production deployment 9ztknibsq in 3m, status Ready
  -> edforge.app HTTP 200, new bundle hash index.975eaed6.js, title preserved

